<h1>quick search</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="stringMatching.html"><em>string matching</em></a> algorithm that compares characters from the end of the search string to its beginning.  When a character doesn't match, the next character in the text beyond the search string determines where the next possible match begins.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="optimalMismatch.html"><em>optimal mismatch</em></a>, <a href="boyermoore.html"><em>Boyer-Moore</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
After <a href="../terms.html#Sund98">[Sund98]</a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Christian Charras' and Thierry Lecroq's <a href="http://www-igm.univ-mlv.fr/~lecroq/string/" target="_blank">Exact String Matching Algorithms (C)</a>

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

